                <pb facs="0824" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/8799: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-11T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1921—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 11—3:25
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Semenoff who is now established at Grodekovo is endeavoring arrange for
                    transportation his troops through Manchuria to Trans-Baikal. If successful this
                    could only result in renewal lawless seizures merchandise and general
                    disorganization of communication with Trans-Baikal. Believe Chinese authorities
                    should be urged not permit Semenoff troops pass through Manchuria.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
